Sample answer:
Let \(A\) be the angle from the horizontal to the top of the billboard and \(B\) the angle to its bottom. Then \(\theta=A-B\), \(\tan A=\frac{a+h}{x}\), and \(\tan B=\frac{h}{x}\).
\(\tan\theta=\tan(A-B)=\frac{\tan A-\tan B}{1+\tan A\tan B}
=\frac{\frac{a+h}{x}-\frac hx}{1+\frac{h(a+h)}{x^2}}
=\frac{ax}{x^2+h(a+h)}\).
Therefore \(\theta=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{ax}{x^2+h(a+h)}\right)\).

